// The other way from ottava-accidental-reminder-2026-10-20.lys (fixed in 1aca41cd2, where Lily# chose
// to print accidentals by the DRAWN place under an octave line). Here the flat is printed under the
// 8vb, on the drawn G2, and the same sounding ges,,, after the line is drawn at G1 with no flat: the
// page reads g,,, there (G1 has had no flat in this bar on the page). LilyPond 2.26.0 draws the same
// (it remembers the sounding pitch), so this is only about Lily#'s own rule of 1aca41cd2: by the drawn
// place, the G1 wants its flat.
// Found by the OMR (S18, 2026-10-20; OmrGen --ottava, seed 11's ledger002 bar 12).
// (lysc 0.14.0 png this file: the ges,,,8 after the line has no flat)
octave absolute
time 4/4
key g major

part p1 { clef bass }

section Piece {
  p1 {
    fis,,16@ottava(bassa) ges,,16 c,,16 c,,16 ges,,8@!ottava r8 r2 |
  }
}

form { ~Piece }

score {
  staff p1 "Staff"
}